---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../site.config';
---

<BaseLayout title="About">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>About {SITE.name}</h1>
    <p>
      <strong>{SITE.name}</strong> is a self-hosted, topic-first knowledge platform — a
      permanent, searchable, linkable home for technical notes, articles, references and
      experiments accumulated across many sources and tools.
    </p>
    <p>
      Content is organised by <em>topic</em> rather than by date. Each topic is a landing
      page that gathers related articles, and every article belongs to a single topic. The
      result is closer to a personal technical wiki than to a chronological blog.
    </p>
    <h2>How it's built</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Astro 5</strong> with content collections for topics and articles.</li>
      <li><strong>MDX</strong> so articles can embed live, interactive components.</li>
      <li><strong>React 19 islands</strong>, hydrated only when scrolled into view.</li>
      <li><strong>Tailwind v4</strong> via the Vite plugin for styling.</li>
      <li><strong>KaTeX</strong> (remark-math + rehype-katex) for mathematics.</li>
      <li><strong>Recharts</strong> for charts and data visualizations.</li>
      <li><strong>Pagefind</strong> for static, scalable full-text search.</li>
      <li><strong>RSS &amp; sitemap</strong> for syndication and SEO.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Everything is static and filesystem-driven: no database, no CMS, no server — just
      content you own, built into plain HTML.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
